  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880378",
      "title": "Disadvantages of Mixins",
      "lectureOrder": 315,
      "videoOrder": 281,
      "sourceHash": "47d50cb9cf9177272a63aeac72f03f35bc2837797e4d8382722fdf70b36f2086",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.12,
          "end": 1.75,
          "en": "Now that were mix ins,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.75,
          "end": 4.93,
          "en": "a very useful mechanism for sharing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.93,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "and functionality across components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 10.55,
          "en": "either across all components with global mix ins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.55,
          "end": 13.22,
          "en": "or across a few selected components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.22,
          "end": 16.67,
          "en": "by manually adding mix ins to components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.67,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "But mix ins have some drawbacks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "or at least one possibly bigger drawback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.01,
          "en": "If you build bigger applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.01,
          "end": 27.16,
          "en": "far bigger than this demo here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.16,
          "end": 29.49,
          "en": "and you're maybe also working in a team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.49,
          "end": 31.41,
          "en": "mix ins can make it harder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 33.64,
          "en": "to understand your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.64,
          "end": 35.29,
          "en": "your component structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.29,
          "end": 37.6,
          "en": "because it's not always obvious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.6,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "where some value is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 43.13,
          "en": "In our alert mix in, we got these show alert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.13,
          "end": 45.19,
          "en": "and hide alert methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.19,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "In our delete user component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "we don't have these methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 51.95,
          "en": "Of course because they are in the mix in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.95,
          "end": 55.69,
          "en": "But we are calling them from inside our template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.69,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "Now, the problem with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "is that here in this simple demo for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.5,
          "end": 62.02,
          "en": "since we're the only developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.02,
          "end": 63.42,
          "en": "who worked on this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.42,
          "end": 65.92,
          "en": "it's obvious where this is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 65.92,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "But think about bigger projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 71.59,
          "en": "where one component maybe is not just using one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.59,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "but let's say five or six mix ins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "And you're maybe also working in a team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 80.25,
          "en": "with many developers working on the code base.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.25,
          "end": 82.73,
          "en": "Then it's not always as obvious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.73,
          "end": 84.4,
          "en": "where something is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 84.4,
          "end": 87.05,
          "en": "If show alert is coming from the alert mix in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.05,
          "end": 89.63,
          "en": "or maybe from the error handling mix in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 89.63,
          "end": 91.4,
          "en": "which you also might have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 91.4,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "And that can be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "With mix ins bigger projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 99.03999999999999,
          "en": "bigger code bases can be harder to manage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 99.03999999999999,
          "end": 100.67,
          "en": "In addition, you have to take care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 100.67,
          "end": 102.32,
          "en": "about this merging behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 102.32,
          "end": 104.35,
          "en": "And in case you have a scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.35,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "where the default merging strategies don't fit you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 109.27000000000001,
          "en": "yes, you can override them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.27000000000001,
          "end": 111.28,
          "en": "but that's a lot of extra care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.28,
          "end": 112.93,
          "en": "you have to take to ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 112.93,
          "end": 114.61,
          "en": "that mix ins work correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 114.61,
          "end": 116.84,
          "en": "And even if they do, you still are left",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 116.84,
          "end": 119.69,
          "en": "with the problem of not immediately seeing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 119.69,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "where some method or where some data piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 124.015,
          "en": "is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 124.015,
          "end": 126.51,
          "en": "That might not be a problem for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 128.27,
          "en": "especially in smaller projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 128.27,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "or if you're working on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "But as I said in bigger projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 132.7,
          "en": "it could be a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 132.7,
          "end": 136.24,
          "en": "and that's why Vue.js has a solution for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 136.24,
          "end": 138.3,
          "en": "and why Vue.js actually has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 138.3,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "an entire alternative way for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 142.84,
          "en": "to write your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 142.84,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "Instead of setting up data, methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 146.8,
          "en": "computed and watches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 146.8,
          "end": 148.79,
          "en": "as you learn it throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 148.79,
          "end": 150.91,
          "en": "Vue offers an alternative way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 150.91,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "the composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "which I already covered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 156.38,
          "en": "in the previous course module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 156.38,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "And you might remember that in that last module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.5,
          "en": "I already mentioned one possible downside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 162.5,
          "end": 164.64,
          "en": "you might face in bigger Vue apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 164.64,
          "end": 166.67000000000002,
          "en": "when using the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 166.67000000000002,
          "end": 168.84,
          "en": "so the way of building components with data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "methods, computed and watch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "which we used in the majority of this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 175.45,
          "en": "It's a great way, but re-using logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 175.45,
          "end": 178.85,
          "en": "can be tricky or cumbersome because we use mix ins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 178.85,
          "end": 182.42,
          "en": "for re-using logic when using that options API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 182.42,
          "end": 184.83,
          "en": "and for the reasons I just mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 187.96,
          "en": "that can be problematic in bigger apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 187.96,
          "end": 190,
          "en": "And with the composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 190,
          "end": 192.75,
          "en": "we have a nicer way of re-using logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 192.75,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "across components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 197.66,
          "en": "Because whilst we have mix ins for sharing logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 197.66,
          "end": 199.57,
          "en": "in the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 199.57,
          "end": 202.03,
          "en": "we have custom composition functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 202.03,
          "end": 204.4,
          "en": "when working with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 204.4,
          "end": 206.323,
          "en": "So let's see how that would work.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
